{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 27,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Job again took up his parable, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As God liveth, who hath taken away my right,\nAnd the Almighty, who hath vexed my soul",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For my life is yet whole in me,\nAnd the spirit of God is in my nostrils);",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely my lips shall not speak unrighteousness,\nNeither shall my tongue utter deceit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Far be it from me that I should justify you:\nTill I die I will not put away mine integrity from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My righteousness I hold fast, and will not let it go:\nMy heart shall not reproach ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " so long as I live.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let mine enemy be as the wicked,\nAnd let him that riseth up against me be as the unrighteous.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For what is the hope of the godless, though he get him gain,\nWhen God taketh away his soul?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will God hear his cry,\nWhen trouble cometh upon him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will he delight himself in the Almighty,\nAnd call upon God at all times?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will teach you concerning the hand of God;\nThat which is with the Almighty will I not conceal.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, all ye yourselves have seen it;\nWhy then are ye become altogether vain?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This is the portion of a wicked man with God,\nAnd the heritage of oppressors, which they receive from the Almighty:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If his children be multiplied, it is for the sword;\nAnd his offspring shall not be satisfied with bread.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Those that remain of him shall be buried in death,\nAnd his widows shall make no lamentation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though he heap up silver as the dust,\nAnd prepare raiment as the clay;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He may prepare it, but the just shall put it on,\nAnd the innocent shall divide the silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He buildeth his house as the moth,\nAnd as a booth which the keeper maketh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He lieth down rich, but he shall not be gathered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to his fathers",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ";\nHe openeth his eyes, and he is not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Terrors overtake him like waters;\nA tempest stealeth him away in the night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The east wind carrieth him away, and he departeth;\nAnd it sweepeth him out of his place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall hurl at him, and not spare:\nHe would fain flee out of his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.27.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.27.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Men shall clap their hands at him,\nAnd shall hiss him out of his place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
